Z||000004||CountFiero||11-18-2001||10:42 PM||||I think the REAL question here is WHY are Fiero door locks so CRA**Y in the first place.  I have an 84 SE and ever since I've owned it the lock cyl. has been screwed up, and I bought it with 35K on it.  These things must have fallen apart as the guy driving out the back door of the factory slammed the door.  Fiero door locks--across the board are S**T.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000005||cadaver||11-20-2001||12:24 AM||||Or maybe Count someone tried to break into it screwing the lock. That is why I had to do one of mine. Jeez some people.||||reg||1
Z||000006||thomas_l||11-20-2001||05:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AEmedic:<BR><B>how did you get the clip to line up, I can't seem to get it in place?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Use a magnet to get it in position then drive it on with a big screwhammer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> might also help to duct tape the cylinder on the outside so it won't push thru the door when you clip it.||||reg||3
